  "about": "Scripted utterances for end-of-turn detection. Each utterance is one intended turn: its fragments are what a recognizer transcribes between pauses, and pauses_ms[i] is the silence after fragment i. A pause at or above the recognizer's stop ends a transcript; a shorter one is bridged. Half are cut mid-clause by a pause long enough to end a transcript; half are complete turns. Authored for this set before anything was measured; transcripts use both punctuated (Whisper-like) and unpunctuated (streaming) styles, and some cuts carry no lexical cue or were punctuated by the recognizer, so the rules are expected to miss them.",
